        <span class="section-label">Founder</span>
        <h2 class="founder-name">Jon Ajinga</h2>
        <div class="founder-role">Designer and developer</div>
        <p>I started Pikes Peak Web Designs because small service businesses kept hearing the same three answers: build it yourself on a website platform, pay $5,000 up front, or pour your content into a template that looks like every other site in your trade. None of those fits a solo plumber, a three-truck HVAC company, or a family roofing business that needs the phone to ring next week.</p>
        <p>So I built something different. I design every site from a blank page, write it in custom code, host it on a fast global network, and look after it myself from the day it goes live. Because I built every part of it, I know what's underneath. If your contact form sends something strange at eight in the evening, you don't file a support ticket with strangers. You tell me, and I fix it.</p>
        <p>A website has a job to do: bring in calls, fill your calendar, and answer common questions before a customer picks up the phone. Everything on this site, from the pricing page to the owner's guide, is published so you can see what you'd get before we talk.</p>
